        "subject": "LU-10499 pcc: set PCC copy mode by cache type",
        "message": "LU-10499 pcc: set PCC copy mode by cache type\n\nPCC created every cache file with mode 0000, whether it was a\nPCC-RO copy that can be dropped at any time, or a PCC-RW copy that\nmay hold the only copy of the file data.  A tool that purges files\nfrom the PCC backend could not tell the two apart.\n\nSet the mode of a PCC-RW copy to 0600 when it is attached or\ncreated, so that a purge tool can skip files with write permission.\nA PCC-RO copy keeps mode 0000.  A PCC-RO attach does not change the\nmode of the PCC file, so that a reused PCC-RW copy, which may still\nbe the HSM archive copy of the file, keeps its write permission.\n\nUsers still cannot access the PCC files directly, since the PCC\ndirectories are created with mode 0000.\n\nAdd sanity-pcc test_46b to check the PCC copy mode.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pcc\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib033762db682522697ad78b40a8733ae9e3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
